# Rule: Format Go Before Building

**Status:** Active
**Date:** 2026-09-03
**Owner:** alex
**Statement:** Always run gofmt on every changed Go file before any build, lint, or test command.
**Scope:** fleet, path:**/*.go
**Enforcement:** Enforced
**Control:** wb pre-commit hook profile go-standard
**Sources:** lesson:kinder-fake-hides-bug, decision:0012
**Why:** An unformatted file reddens CI on a cosmetic diff and hides the real failure underneath it.
**Exceptions:** Generated files under gen/, by the owner of the generator only.
**Supersedes:** older-gofmt-rule
**Superseded By:** —

## Instructions

Run `gofmt -l .`; if it lists anything, run `gofmt -w` on those files before continuing.

Applies to: skill:go-hygiene

## Examples

### Compliant

```sh
gofmt -w ./pkg/rule && go build ./...
```

### Violation

```sh
go build ./... # with an unformatted file still staged
```

## Open Questions

None at this time.

